    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Galaxy_at_War\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War\">Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War</a></i> </p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Hazards\" title=\"Hazards\">Hazards</a>, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Poisons\" title=\"Poisons\">Poisons</a></i> </p><p>Trauger is a&nbsp;volcanic toxin&nbsp;created by underground&nbsp;pressure vents on&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Socorro\" title=\"Socorro\">Socorro</a>. Exposure to trauger results in horrific effects; nausea, vertigo, respiratory failure, convulsions, muscle impairment, blurred vision, or even cardiac arrest could occur. </p><h2><span id=\"Trauger_Statistics_.28CL_14.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trauger_Statistics_(CL_14)\">Trauger Statistics (CL 14)</span></h2><p><b><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Keywords\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Keywords\">Keywords</a>:</b> Atmosphere, Natural, Poison </p><p><b>Trigger:</b> A creature is exposed to Trauger. </p><p><b>Attack:</b> +16 vs <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fortitude_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fortitude Defense\">Fortitude Defense</a> </p><p><b>Recurrence:</b> Each round at the start of the target's turn, as long as the target remains exposed to Trauger. </p>",
